<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Jan-Sept trade gap rises to CZK 110.7 bln.</title>
<headline>Czech Jan-Sept trade gap rises to CZK 110.7 bln.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech trade balance for the first nine months in 1996 rose to 110.7 billion crowns from a revised deficit of 100.2 billion for the January-August period, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The trade deficit for the January-September period in 1995 was 62.3 billion crowns.  </p>
